Q: How to find a element inside a DIV with Selenium WebDriver A: <p>You can use below CSS selector to get the text.</p>

<pre><code> driver.FindElement(By.CssSelector("body &gt; fieldset:nth-child(1) &gt; div:nth-child(2) &gt; div:nth-child(2) &gt; span:nth-child(3)"));
</code></pre>

<p>Edit</p>

<pre><code>var element =  driver.FindElement(By.CssSelector("fieldset:nth-child(1) &gt; div:nth-child(2) &gt; div:nth-child(2) &gt; span"));
string v = element.Text;
</code></pre>
